    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The mean price of bags of potatoes at different supermarkets was $\\$4.50$. The sum of the data was $\\$90.00$. How many bags of potatoes were included in the survey?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "20 bags",
      "worked": "The number of bags is the total of the prices divided by the mean price.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of bags}&=\\frac{90.00}{4.50}\\\\\\text{Number of bags}&=20\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere were 20 bags of potatoes in the survey.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
